WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome, everyone,
welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.834
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:04.567
You're here.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.767
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:08.367
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:11.868
I want to wish everyone a happy
St. Patrick's Day to you there.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:15.567
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:18.033
Yeah, St. Patrick's
is a major holiday.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.000
In fact, all the banks
were closed today,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.100
although that had nothing to do
with St. Patrick's Day.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:25.801
Yeah, everyone's talking
about this --

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.367
following the recent
bank crashes,

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.167
President Biden
has asked Congress

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.067
for more authority
to punish bank executives.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.801
[ Oohs ]
-Then Bernie Sanders

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.200
picked up some brass knuckles
and said --

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.200
[ As Sanders ]
Or I can just handle it myself.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:40.734
Biden's had it.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.100
It's like a movie detective
who puts his badge in the drawer

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.801
and goes,
"I'm not a cop tonight."

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.300
Yeah, Biden isn't
messing around.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.200
Apparently, he wants
to punish the bank CEOs

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.501
by chaining all their pens
to the desk.

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:57.267
Some more big news -- I read
that law enforcement agencies

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.934
are preparing
for the possibility that,

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.200
as early as next week,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.701
former President Trump
could be indicted.

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:06.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:08.534
Which is why Trump
is currently packing

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.234
for spring break in Switzerland.

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:11.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.300
I think even Trump
knows it's coming

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.067
because today he was walking
around in a green shirt

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.501
that said,
"Kiss me, I'm indicted."

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:18.000
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.734
-At this point, Trump has
so many legal problems,

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.467
everyone's filling out brackets
for which one finally gets him.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.234
[ Laughter ]
They're like Stormy Daniels

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:25.701
versus Georgia election
tampering.

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.000
I don't know.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.033
Did you guys see this?

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.267
According to a new poll,
49% of Americans

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.234
would support banning TikTok.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:34.100
[ Boos and nos ]

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.300
Yeah, that's pretty much half.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.200
And, apparently,
even people on TikTok are split

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.234
on whether to ban the app.
-Really?!

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.000
[ Laughter ]
-I think it's pretty clear why.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.767
For example, this user
doesn't want to ban TikTok.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.501
-3, 2, 1.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:48.501
[ Explosions ]

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.467
[ Cheering ]

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.200
Yeah, while this user does.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.334
[ Hip hop plays ]

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:58.033
[ Ohhs, laughter, and applause ]

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:03.267
Here's another example.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.267
This user doesn't want
to ban TikTok.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.100
-[Indistinct]

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.000
[ Awws ]

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.634
Yeah.
But this user does.

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:10.300
-YOLO.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:12.701
-[Indistinct]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.634
-Aah!

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
-You took the whole house!

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.734
[ Cheering ]
-Wow! The whole thing.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.067
He's still in the slide.
-He's still in the slide.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:26.767
-Yeah, yeah,
he's living in there, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.167
And, finally, this user
doesn't want to ban TikTok.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:30.300
-1, 2, 3.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.000
-[ Inhaling sharply ]

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:35.234
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, while this user does.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:36.334
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:37.567
-[ Inhales sharply ]

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.501
[ Laughter, ohhs, and applause ]

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.400
-Oh!

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:46.868
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.033
[Indistinct]

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:52.167
Well, guys, March Madness is
in full swing

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:55.434
and one of the big upsets,
so far, was 15 seed Princeton

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.934
knocking off number 2 Arizona.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:03:00.634
[ Ohhs, cheering, and applause ]

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:03.601
Everyone in Princeton
was acting pretty cocky

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:05.033
and that was even
before the game started.

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.734
-Oh.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:08.467
-Some business news --
I saw that IKEA

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:10.300
has recalled thousands
of mirrors

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.200
because they could fall
and cut people.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.434
-[ Snickers ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.968
Honestly, customers should've
seen this coming

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:19.133
because the name
of the mirror is

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:20.467
"Fall and cut you."

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:21.367
[ Laughter and applause ]
There you go.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.868
That's "Valunkutu."

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:26.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.000
You guys, get this --
7-Eleven just announced

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.734
that they are launching
a huge new

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:34.133
electric vehicle
charging network.

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.767
It's perfect if you've ever been
at 7-Eleven and thought,

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:38.367
"I want to stay here
for 60 minutes.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:41.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.200
I want to stay here
for more than ten minutes."

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.667
It sounds high-tech,
but all they do is

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.334
plug your Tesla
into the hot dog roller.

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.434
-Really?
-Yeah, that's right.

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:51.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:54.000
That's right, you fill your car
up at 7-Eleven,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.701
then, an hour later,
the car gets heartburn.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.467
[ Laughter ]
It's interesting.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.734
Guys, listen to this --
according to new research,

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:03.167
horseback riding could actually
help ease back pain.

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:04.167
[ Murmuring ]

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.901
Unless, of course,
you're the horse.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:08.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.601
Finally, you guys,
I'm very excited.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.100
It is St. Patrick's Day today.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:14.868
I mean, this is a big deal.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.934
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:19.400
I love it.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.467
But I got to say, every year,
people focus too much

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:24.000
on the stereotypes
and not enough on what makes,

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.567
really, St. Patrick's Day
and Ireland so special

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.767
and, to show you what I mean,
I actually wrote a little song.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:29.901
Roots, can I get a note?

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.434
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.467
[ Irish accent ]
♪ Oh oh ♪

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:35.601
♪ The 17th of March is here ♪

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.667
♪ The day has got me thinkin' ♪

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.667
♪ St. Patty's Day and Ireland ♪

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:42.567
♪ So much more than drinkin' ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:44.167
♪ The cliffs of Moher
are gorgeous ♪

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:46.267
♪ If great heights
you do not fear ♪

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.133
♪ A lovely place
to see the view ♪

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.033
♪ And crack an ice cold...
water ♪

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.968
♪ Go and see the Blarney Stone ♪

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.868
♪ And kiss it,
if you're frisky ♪

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:58.100
♪ Then wash your mouth out
with a giant shot ♪

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.467
♪ Of Irish...LaCroix ♪

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.300
♪ There are no snakes
on Emerald Isle ♪

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.234
♪ No creepy crawly scalies ♪

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.400
♪ So, just relax,
enjoy some coffee ♪

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.467
♪ Mixed with creamy oat milk ♪

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:10.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.868
♪ Pick a four-leaf clover
hidden underneath a shrub ♪

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:15.567
♪ Then show it off
to all your mates ♪

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.167
♪ Down at the local library ♪

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:21.767
♪ To Dublin or to Galway,
if you want to see a sight ♪

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:24.834
♪ And watch two old men argue
till it turns into a... ♪

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.901
Cordial acceptance
of their differences.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:29.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:32.701
[ Cheering ]

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.801
♪ Now, my tune is over ♪

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.868
♪ Time to climb into me bunk ♪

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:41.434
♪ That's all to say
this St. Patrick's Day ♪

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.300
♪ Screw it, let's get drunk ♪

